## Why this region exists

`capture_image_with_Bulb` (the `stage2_region` fixture) does not contain the
message-driven stop edge that lifecycle cases 1–4 assert on. It was traced in
the retained source ELF:

- `stopCaptureImageForMessage` (`0x202e4`, 108 bytes) is called from exactly two
  places: `captureBulbImage` and `sonyBurstEvent`.
- `gp_camera_stop_timeout` (`0x35158`) has one caller, `gp_camera_exit`.
- `gp_context_cancel` (`0x358d0`) has 27 call sites, all libgphoto-internal.

`captureBulbImage` is therefore the function that owns the edge, and it also
calls `capture_image_with_Bulb` at `0x206e0`. Cases 1–4 are re-pointed here via
`preferred_fixture`.

## Retrieval

The source ELF is retained in the private research repository:

```
PrivateResearch firmware-packets/6.0.0.54.90--o-v18m-k1ii-pgphoto-readiness-20261029/
  extracted_appfs/stage2-ondisk/ondisk/pgphoto.stage2ondisk
```

Extract the region (symbol vaddr `0x20604`, `.text` file offset `0x10604`):

```bash
dd if=pgphoto.stage2ondisk bs=1 skip=$((0x10604)) count=684 status=none \
  > tests/fixtures/arm/capture_bulb_image_region.bin
sha256sum tests/fixtures/arm/capture_bulb_image_region.bin
# 9917d69fc9228d2234e9e735cd3ad3c102941ebfb501de3c91681a695517073e
```

The harness refuses to run the fixture if the on-disk bytes do not match the
SHA-256 recorded in `capture_bulb_image_region.json`.

## Layout

Load at the original vaddr (`load_address: 0x20604`). The function resolves
globals with `ldr rN, [pc, #imm]` followed by `add rN, pc, rN`, whose literal
pool words are PC-relative deltas — loading at a relocated base makes those
loads compute unrelated addresses. `code_address: 0x20000` /
`code_size: 0x300000` map a page-aligned range covering the blob and its
referenced globals (`.rodata` `0x25cfb0`, `0x25d070`; `.dynamic` `0x2f6ffc`).

## Call targets

All 17 BL sites resolved from the retained ELF — 9 via `.symtab` FUNC entries,
8 via `.rel.plt` → `.dynsym`:

| callee | stub group | sites |
|---|---|---|
| `textdomain` (PLT) | os | 3 |
| `getValueWithSeetingsForKey` | os | 2 |
| `pthread_cond_signal` (PLT) | os | 2 |
| `pthread_getspecific` (PLT) | os | 2 |
| `getSettingsValueForKey` | os | 1 |
| `qsort` (PLT) | os | 1 |
| `HI_LOG_Print` | os | 1 |
| `sp_async_thread_function` | callback | 1 |
| `capture_image_with_Bulb` | camera | 1 |
| `stopCaptureImageForMessage` | camera | 1 |
| `camera_preview_enable` | camera | 1 |
| `checkCameraStatus` | camera | 1 |

Boundary aliases recorded in the sidecar: `stop` and `message_stop` both map to
`stopCaptureImageForMessage`. There is no counterpart to `context_cancel` or
`close` in this function.

## Current limitation (recorded, not hidden)

Measured with the committed sidecar config: **84 instructions, 10 boundary
calls** (including `capture_image_with_Bulb`), then
`UC_ERR_READ_UNMAPPED` at `0x20750`. The preceding `ldr r3, [r4, r3]` loads a
`.rodata` string address and the code dereferences it as a pointer, which only
makes sense with the real global contents and a populated caller frame.

`stopCaptureImageForMessage` is called at `0x207e8`, **beyond** that fault. So
the stop edge is present in this region but not reachable by straight-line
execution yet. Closing the gap needs:

1. the referenced `.rodata`/`.data` words mapped with their real contents, and
2. AAPCS argument setup for `captureBulbImage`'s parameters.

Until then, cases 1–4 report the edge as unreachable rather than absent — see
the per-case note naming the call site and fault address.
